<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ciudad Real</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ciudad Real is a city in Castile-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-mancha">La Mancha</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and the capital of the province of the same name. King Alfonso X founded it in 1255 as Villa Real to strengthen royal power in La Mancha against the military orders, and it became a city in 1420. In antiquity its region lay between the lands of the Carpetani, Oretani and Olcades.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ciudad-real.jpg" alt="Ciudad Real" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zarateman · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudad_Real_-_Plaza_Mayor_04_edited.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
